,title,link,text,language,family
0,Kurumba languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kurumba_languages,"Kurumba languages are distinct from Malayalam, Tamil, and Kannada, and linguistic analyses indicate that they retain several features characteristic of Proto-Dravidian.","Kurumba, Kannada",Dravidian
1,Betta Kurumba language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Betta_Kurumba_language,"The Betta Kurumba language (Beṭṭa Kurumba, IPA: [beʈːɐ kurumbɐ]) is a Dravidian language closely related to Kannada and Tamil, [1][2] and is spoken by 32,000 people in the Nilgiri mountains and in adjoining areas in Tamil Nadu, Karnataka and Kerala. Beṭṭa (ಬೆಟ್ಟ) means ""hills"" in Kannada and kurumba (ಕುರುಬ) means ""shepherd"".","Kurumba, Kannada",Dravidian
2,KURUMBA KANNADA SONGS - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLqS0hlU_nnhqpPHyUkdrVPw5C2x4qjDsr,10 முந்தால மாத்தாங்க இத்தோரு | Munthala Manthanga Ithoru Kurumba Kannada Christian Network • 350 views • 8 months ago 2,"Kurumba, Kannada",Dravidian
3,Kurumba languages — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/kurumba_languages,"The Kurumba languages form a cluster of closely related, endangered varieties within the South Dravidian I branch of the Dravidian language family, spoken primarily by small indigenous Kurumba tribal communities in the Nilgiri Hills and surrounding forested regions of southern India, spanning the states of Tamil Nadu, Kerala, and Karnataka. [1] [2] These languages exhibit archaic phonological ...","Kurumba, Kannada",Dravidian
4,Kurumba languages - Wikiwand,https://www.wikiwand.com/en/Kurumba_languages,"Kurumba, refers to a group of languages within the Southern Dravidian branch of the Dravidian language family These languages are spoken by the Kurumba communities, who inhabit Nilgiri Hills, in Tamil Nadu and nearby areas including of Coimbatore, Pudukottai etc. The cultural identity of the Kurumba people is expressed extensively through oral traditions, folklore, and music.","Kurumba, Kannada",Dravidian
5,Kurumba (Father's Love) - YouTube Music,https://music.youtube.com/watch?v=b-xTp4FsBFM&list=RDAMVM5PeOMpYc_QE,Provided to YouTube by Sony Music Entertainment India Pvt. Ltd. Kurumba (Father's Love) · D. Imman · Sid Sriram · Madhan Karky Tik Tik Tik (Original Motion...,"Kurumba, Kannada",Dravidian
6,Archiving Songs and Dance of the Jenu Kurumba Tribe from Karnataka,https://www.academia.edu/68301692/Archiving_Songs_and_Dance_of_the_Jenu_Kurumba_Tribe_from_Karnataka,"Jenu K urumba, also known as Jen Kurumba is a southern Dravidian language of the Tamil-Kannada subgroup spoken by the Jenu K urumba tribe. It is often considered to constitute a dialect of Kannada; however, Ethnologue classifies it as a separate language.","Kurumba, Kannada",Dravidian
7,Kurumba languages - Wikiwand,https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Kurumba_language,"Kurumba languages are distinct from Malayalam, Tamil, and Kannada, and linguistic analyses indicate that they retain several features characteristic of Proto-Dravidian.","Kurumba, Kannada",Dravidian
8,Kurumba - DOBES,https://dobes.mpi.nl/projects/kurumba/,"Their languages belong to the South branch of Dravidian, but further identification or sub-classification is problematic. The project contains audio and visual data on the languages: narrations, songs, interviews, elicitation sessions, etc. and on the cultural events: hunting/fishing, daily occupations, rituals, dance…","Kurumba, Kannada",Dravidian
9,Betta Kuruba - sanchika.ciil.org,https://sanchika.ciil.org/communities/f471779a-3400-4462-981d-c95b041550b4,"Betta Kuruba Betta Kuruba (ISO-639-3 code: xub) Betta Kuruba, also known as Betta Kurumba, is a language belonging to the Southern Dravidian subgroup of the Dravidian language family. It is primarily spoken by the Betta Kurumba, an indigenous tribal community residing in the forested areas of the Nilgiri Hills and surrounding regions.","Kurumba, Kannada",Dravidian
